From: openEuler RISC-V packaging <packaging@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Declare shared state extern in internal headers
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later with the original static-linking exception
Origin: package-local static source review, not an upstream commit
Root-Cause: Header tentative definitions become multiple definitions with modern
 GCC -fno-common. roxml_mem.c already owns head_cell and roxml_core.c already
 owns the three __DEBUG counters. Optional original test libraries use __DEBUG.
Fix: Change only four header declarations to extern; retain their initialized
 definitions, all defaults, test bodies and normal compiler hardening flags.
Removal: Drop when upstream provides equivalent single-definition declarations.
Validation: Pure textual review only here; target build and all original tests
 remain required. No local upstream compilation or execution was performed.
--- a/src/roxml_mem.h
+++ b/src/roxml_mem.h
@@ -17 +17 @@
-memory_cell_t head_cell;
+extern memory_cell_t head_cell;
--- a/src/roxml_core.h
+++ b/src/roxml_core.h
@@ -18,3 +18,3 @@
-unsigned int _nb_node;
-unsigned int _nb_attr;
-unsigned int _nb_text;
+extern unsigned int _nb_node;
+extern unsigned int _nb_attr;
+extern unsigned int _nb_text;
